{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Of that which comes to his hand.</b> From what his hand has acquired — from what comes, and not from robbery, as it is said (Malachi 1:13): ״והבאתם גזול את הפסח ואת החולה והבאתם את המנחה הארצה אותה מידכם״." "<b>Or</b> it may be that <b>of that which comes to his hand</b> means precious stones and pearls." "<b>And there are those</b> who explained <b>of that which comes to his hand</b> as the bird called bar-shonagi (the hunter-bird), for since Esau was a man of the hunt, he brought him this bird with which he would hunt. And accordingly the parsing of the verse is: ״ויקח מנחה לעשו אחיו מן הבא בידו״ — 'and he took a gift for Esau his brother, from that which comes to his hand' — for the word בידו ('in his hand') refers back to Esau, meaning: from what he was accustomed to bring in his hand."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The verse quoted appears to conflate phrases from Malachi 1:13–14; rendered as found in the source without correction."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:53.394984454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}